<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">South Sudan</h1><p class="st-meta">2011 CE – present · capital Juba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Landlocked East African state that separated from Sudan on 9 July 2011 and was drawn into civil war in 2013; a unity government was formed in 2020.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Comprehensive Peace Agreement ended the Second Sudanese Civil War in 2005, a referendum held from 9 to 15 January 2011 gave 98.83% for separation from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sudan">Sudan</a>. South Sudan became independent on 9 July 2011 under President Salva Kiir, and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> five days later. Disputes over oil revenue and the region of Abyei remained.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In December 2013 a power struggle between Kiir and his former deputy Riek Machar began the South Sudanese Civil War. About 400,000 people are estimated to have been killed and more than 4 million displaced, with fighting along ethnic lines. A peace agreement of 2015 broke down, and a deal on 20 February 2020 formed a unity government with Machar as First Vice-President. A transitional constitution of 2011 sets up a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/presidential-democracy">presidential system</a>. The country joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-community">East African Community</a> in 2016. Violence between armed groups has continued.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Elections due in 2023 were postponed, first to 2024 and then to December 2026. Machar was arrested on 26 March 2025 on Kiir's orders, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Secretary-General said the peace agreement was in shambles. Kiir dissolved the transitional government on 24 September 2026, with elections set for 22 December.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/south-sudan.jpg" alt="South Sudan" width="330" height="165"><figcaption>Image: Achim1999 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Sudan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2